PN,41101
SC,0001
CT,2,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F411A1786465168
OL,3,CMoon to cover 90% of sun in 'deepest
OL,4,Ceclipse until 2090'
OL,6,FViewing events have been planned to
OL,7,Ftake place across the island of
OL,8,FIreland ahead of what is expected to
OL,9,Fbe the "deepest eclipse" over local
OL,10,Fskies until 2090.
OL,12,FThe Moon is set to cover more than 90%
OL,13,Fof the Sun in a partial solar eclipse
OL,14,Fon Wednesday evening.
OL,16,FIt is described as likely to be the
OL,17,Fdeepest eclipse seen from the region
OL,18,Fsince the total eclipse of August 1999
OL,19,Fand the last time that such an eclipse
OL,20,Fwill be seen here until 2090.
OL,26,@qD@HOUqD@XO]
OL,1,W~k4 jw=hw1 hw}h7}j7}            G1/6
OL,2,W/*% /*%/"-$+,*%/*%/*-'T(,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,23,TppppppppppppppppppGsource: itv.com/news
OL,24,ANext Page BNI NewsCClean Feed FThis Day
FL,412,410,140,120,000,100
PN,41102
SC,0002
CT,2,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F411A1786465168
OL,3,CMoon to cover 90% of sun in 'deepest
OL,4,Ceclipse until 2090'
OL,6,FSome areas of the world are expected
OL,7,Fto see a total eclipse, including
OL,8,Fparts of Spain, Greenland and Iceland.
OL,10,FQueen's University Belfast has planned
OL,11,Fevents for the public as well as the
OL,12,FArmagh Observatory and Planetarium.
OL,13,FThey are hosting a day of activities
OL,14,Ffrom 10am to 8pm, including hands-on
OL,15,Fscience demonstrations, dome shows and
OL,16,Feclipse-themed events for all ages.
OL,18,FDirector of Armagh Observatory and
OL,19,FPlanetarium, Professor Michael Burton,
OL,20,Fdescribed one of the most eagerly
OL,21,Fawaited eclipses for decades.
OL,1,W~k4 jw=hw1 hw}h7}j7}            G2/6
OL,2,W/*% /*%/"-$+,*%/*%/*-'T(,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,23,TppppppppppppppppppGsource: itv.com/news
OL,24,ANext Page BNI NewsCClean Feed FThis Day
FL,412,410,140,120,000,100
PN,41103
SC,0003
CT,2,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F411A1786465168
OL,3,CMoon to cover 90% of sun in 'deepest
OL,4,Ceclipse until 2090'
OL,6,F"While we won't encounter totality
OL,7,Fhere ` only a narrow path across
OL,8,FGreenland, Iceland and northern Spain
OL,9,Fwill be fortunate enough to encounter
OL,10,Fthis ` a 94% partial eclipse is an
OL,11,Fextraordinary sight in its own right,"
OL,12,Fhe said.
OL,14,F"At its peak, the Sun will be reduced
OL,15,Fto the thinnest sliver of light, low
OL,16,Fover the western horizon. It is going
OL,17,Fto be a beautiful and quite eerie
OL,18,Fspectacle."
OL,26,@nD@AOUsD@fO]vD@AOUzD@KO]
OL,1,W~k4 jw=hw1 hw}h7}j7}            G3/6
OL,2,W/*% /*%/"-$+,*%/*%/*-'T(,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,23,TppppppppppppppppppGsource: itv.com/news
OL,24,ANext Page BNI NewsCClean Feed FThis Day
FL,412,410,140,120,000,100
PN,41104
SC,0004
CT,2,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F411A1786465168
OL,3,CMoon to cover 90% of sun in 'deepest
OL,4,Ceclipse until 2090'
OL,6,FHe said the eclipse will begin at
OL,7,Fapproximately 6.10pm, reaching its
OL,8,Fmaximum at around 7.08pm and
OL,9,Fconcluding shortly after 8pm.
OL,11,FObservers can expect to see a striking
OL,12,Fscene, with the crescent Sun glowing
OL,13,Flow in the evening sky.
OL,15,FProf Burton added: "The last time
OL,16,Fskies over Ireland darkened to this
OL,17,Fextent was in 1999. On that occasion
OL,18,Fpeople travelled from all over to
OL,19,Fstand under the path of totality in
OL,20,FCornwall.
OL,26,@wD@TOU
OL,1,W~k4 jw=hw1 hw}h7}j7}            G4/6
OL,2,W/*% /*%/"-$+,*%/*%/*-'T(,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,23,TppppppppppppppppppGsource: itv.com/news
OL,24,ANext Page BNI NewsCClean Feed FThis Day
FL,412,410,140,120,000,100
PN,41105
SC,0005
CT,2,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F411A1786465168
OL,3,CMoon to cover 90% of sun in 'deepest
OL,4,Ceclipse until 2090'
OL,6,F"You don't need to travel anywhere
OL,7,Fthis time ` history is coming to us."
OL,9,FHe reminded viewers to never look
OL,10,Fdirectly at the Sun during the partial
OL,11,Feclipse.
OL,13,F"The Sun is never safe to look at
OL,14,Fdirectly with the naked eye,
OL,15,Fbinoculars or a camera, no matter how
OL,16,Fmuch of it is covered by the Moon," he
OL,17,Fsaid.
OL,26,@nD@AOUoD@eO]uD@AOUxD@cO]
OL,1,W~k4 jw=hw1 hw}h7}j7}            G5/6
